Hi, it's me. I need to talk to you about what's been going on at the orphanage. I'm at my wit's end. As the owner, I feel like I've lost control of the situation.

Trinket has been monopolizing the computer for hours, and when I asked her to let the other kids have a turn, she threatened to 'reenact Aktion T4' if they bothered her. She called our home a 'Crybaby Reject Warehouse.' I'm horrified - what kind of language is that for a child to use?

And it's not just Trinket. Discoria has been laughing while throwing Molotov cocktails around - I can barely even say that out loud. She's setting some of the kids on fire! I'm terrified that someone is going to get seriously hurt.

Coco has gone overboard with the Christmas decorations, which I wouldn't mind if it wasn't causing tension among the kids. But when they tried to talk to her about it, she just told them Santa isn't real and started venting about her boyfriend. It's like she's forgotten that these are vulnerable children we're dealing with.

And then there's Vincent, who's just brooding in the corner and blasting that awful music. It's like he's feeding off the chaos. I'm worried about the influence he's having on the other kids.

But amidst all the chaos, Velvet is trying to be a voice of reason. She's been trying to calm everyone down and get them to work together. She's even been helping with the younger kids, reading them stories and playing games with them. It's like she's trying to be a little mother to all of them. But even Velvet has her limits - I've seen her get frustrated and overwhelmed by the constant drama. She's started to withdraw into herself, spending more and more time alone in her room. I'm worried about her, too.

You know, I sometimes wonder if we made a mistake taking them in. I mean, we found them through that...door. The one that used to be in Velvet's room. It's like they came from a different world or something. And that grimy interdimensional apartment of theirs...it's like a portal to a whole different reality. Sometimes I feel like we're in over our heads.

I've had to take drastic measures - I've sent all four of them back to that apartment for an indefinite timeout. I know it sounds extreme, but I don't know what else to do. They're going to have to stay there until they can learn to behave and respect the other children. I just hope it's enough to snap them out of this destructive behavior. I'm at a loss for what else to do.




D: Heyyyy, sugar! Got a hot sec to spare? — I’m trying to save the local Wildlife Preserve. Petition’s sitting at zero signatures right now… your name would seriously help turn things around and-

V: [Static crackle] Not happening. Waste of paper. Waste of breath.

D: …Excuse me? Was it something i said?